2.0.0
* Implemented VModem Multi-DTE support:
 * implemented udev rules to trigger dynamically on serial USB hotplug events
 * implemented new service instance unit file for systemd to support
   multiple USB serial adapters
 * adapted setup.sh for new system/udev config files
* Relocated network setup to dependant unit service vmodem-network
 * it's spawned when first serial USB device is plugged
 * it's stopped when last serial USB device is unplugged
* Implemented CNI host-local as leightweight IPAM to
  coordinate IP address assignments and revocations for ppp.sh
  accross multiple instances
* implemented port-bound configuration file support
* implemented port-bound support for baud & emulation profiles
* added default_speaker_mode to enforce ATM0 for ISDN emulation
* did some code cleanups and reorganization in vmodem.sh
* implemented traffic shaper
* extended ppp.sh to emit tc status every 60 seconds
* implemented common `vmodem` journald namespace with 100 MB limit
* added new configuration menu to allow persistent changes to
  baud rates, modem emulation, PPP settings, and more
* added support to toggle DCD mode (default: DCD enabled)
  (Trumpet Winsock bugfix)
* implemented centralized vmodem-soundd daemon to support Multi-DTE setups
* implemented silent mode support in vmodem-soundd to support silent dial-in
* adapted vmodem.sh to use vmodem-soundd instead of sound.py
* removed sound.py
* replaced 10.0.100.0/24 RFC1918 by 100.64.254.0/24 RFC6598
  to not cause overlaps within LANs. One should not use this one normally
  on local sites, but since TPC-Vmodem is essentially also emulating an
  ISP PPP headend, it's safe. Plus it's in preparation for an upcoming feature.
* restructured the repository and /opt/vmodem into a UNIX-like layout
  (bin/, libexec/, etc/, share/, tools/); per-port configurations moved
  from /opt/vmodem/config to /opt/vmodem/etc/portconfig
* replaced setup.sh's per-file download facility by git clone/pull,
  and replaced copied system files (systemd units, udev rules, journald
  config) by symlinks into /opt/vmodem/etc, so a git pull updates
  everything in place
* introduced centralized defaults.conf for config definitions in vmodem.sh
  and ppp.sh: the two scripts now only include fallback declarations
  for sanity reasons. 
* extracted shared configuration and SETUP menus into lib/vmodem/common.inc
* added console configurator bin/vmodem-config.sh with optional instance restart
* added layered global/per-port overrides and consistent ATZ/AT&F reset defaults
* added a declarative NetworkManager profile for VISP infrastructure on visp0,
  activated and deactivated with the shared VModem network service
* README updates
* replaced iptables and the network shell script with declarative nftables tables
  for subscriber NAT/forwarding and VISP services
* added 3proxy from its signed APT repository for synthetic DNS and HTTP forwarding,
  using the packaged service with VISP configuration and shared network lifecycle
* added per-modem Transparent DNS/HTTP Proxy configuration with global and per-port
  overrides, propagated to the selected dial script
* added a local VISP web server on 100.64.255.180, served by 3proxy
* reworked setup.sh, added check_os() boiler-plate, especially as TPC-VModem is
  not yet currently ready for Debain 13
